title:
Photo polymer printing plates have a light sensitive emulsion that hardens when it gets exposed to ultraviolet light. The rest of the emulsion that does not get exposed washes away with water using a soft brush.

//

Prior to developing your plate you would need to invert your design and print it as dark and opaque as possible onto a transparency. Once your design is printed you can then place it on top of your photo polymer printing plate and expose it to ultraviolet light.

//

The length of time that you need to expose is determined by the intensity of the light source that you're using. For example, if you're using the sunlight then you would expose for around 6 to 10 minutes, if you're using an artificial light source such as an LED black light you would expose for somewhere in the neighborhood of a minute and a half. 

//

Making stamps using photopolymer printing plates is a great alternative to investing thousands of dollars into 3D printers, CNC routers, or laser engravers. 

//

